{
 "thread": "VDpKs1yGb9c",
 "subject": "system config to fully isolate from CRAN/use only a local CRAN-like repository",
 "messages_listed": 5,
 "last_activity": "2015-01-23T02:43:42Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "frvigSaloJEJ",
   "from": "Yasmin Lucero",
   "author": "cd47ca3bbd96bb85",
   "date": "2015-01-22T19:09:06Z",
   "subject": "system config to fully isolate from CRAN/use only a local CRAN-like repository",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve seen this: <div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242671593000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0SNfNsKOxhAu0WmMxkKtKg\">http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>But this requires me to set my repo option after initializing a new project. I would like to be able to set a system configuration so that all new projects default to only knowing about our local repository, unless explicitly told about an external CRAN mirror. Packrat seems to stomp on my system .Rprofile file. Am I missing something?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "hUwmoP_4fxEJ",
   "from": "Kevin Ushey",
   "author": "ab0d2be2ea8dabe8",
   "date": "2015-01-22T23:56:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: system config to fully isolate from CRAN/use only a local CRAN-like repository",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi Yasmin,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">When initializing a new project, packrat infers the repositories based on the current value of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">getOption(&#39;repos&#39;)</code>, and then caches those (in the lockfile) to be used later.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">It seems like you would be able to do such a thing with e.g. <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">options(repos = &lt;localRepos); packrat::init()</code>.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">For example, if I run:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">R --vanilla --slave -e &quot;options(repos = &#39;~/local/cran&#39;); packrat::init()&quot;\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I see in the generated lockfile:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">Repos: CRAN=~/local/cran\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">It sounds like this (or some version of this) should suffice for what you need.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Best,<br>Kevin</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgWWFzbWluLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+V2hlbiBpbml0aWFsaXppbmcgYSBuZXcgcHJv\r\namVjdCwgcGFja3JhdCBpbmZlcnMgdGhlIHJlcG9zaXRvcmllcyBiYXNlZCBvbiB0aGUgY3VycmVu\r\ndCB2YWx1ZSBvZiBgZ2V0T3B0aW9uKCdyZXBvcycpYCwgYW5kIHRoZW4gY2FjaGVzIHRob3NlIChp\r\nbiB0aGUgbG9ja2ZpbGUpIHRvIGJlIHVzZWQgbGF0ZXIuPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj5JdCBzZWVtcyBsaWtlIHlvdSB3b3VsZCBiZSBhYmxlIHRvIGRvIHN1Y2ggYSB0aGluZyB3aXRo\r\nIGUuZy4gYG9wdGlvbnMocmVwb3MgPSAmbHQ7bG9jYWxSZXBvcyk7IHBhY2tyYXQ6OmluaXQoKWAu\r\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5Gb3IgZXhhbXBsZSwgaWYgSSBydW46PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7IFIgLS12YW5pbGxhIC0tc2xhdmUgLWUgIm9w\r\ndGlvbnMocmVwb3MgPSAnfi9sb2NhbC9jcmFuJyk7IHBhY2tyYXQ6OmluaXQoKSI8L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pkkgc2VlIGluIHRoZSBnZW5lcmF0ZWQgbG9ja2ZpbGU6PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7IFJlcG9zOiBDUkFOPX4vbG9jYWwvY3Jhbjwv\r\nZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+SXQgc291bmRzIGxpa2UgdGhpcyAob3Igc29tZSB2ZXJz\r\naW9uIG9mIHRoaXMpIHNob3VsZCBzdWZmaWNlIGZvciB3aGF0IHlvdSBuZWVkLjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+\r\nPGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+QmVzdCw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PktldmluPC9kaXY+\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
