    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve seen this: <div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242671595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2v5Gc-wGI1qZwgGuLKxTqL\">http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>But this requires me to set my repo option after initializing a new project. I would like to be able to set a system configuration so that all new projects default to only knowing about our local repository, unless explicitly told about an external CRAN mirror. Packrat seems to stomp on my system .Rprofile file. Am I missing something?</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
