   "subject": "Re: system config to fully isolate from CRAN/use only a local CRAN-like repository",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Right — alternatively, you could add something to your project-local .Rprofile like:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">if (file.exists(&quot;~/.Rprofile&quot;)) source(&quot;~/.Rprofile&quot;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">or we could even consider allowing users to opt-in to sourcing <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">~/.Rprofile</code> on <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::init()</code> (ie, automatically adding that code to the auto-loader), but this does break isolation a bit.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:UmlnaHQgLS0gYWx0ZXJuYXRpdmVseSwgeW91IGNvdWxkIGFkZCBzb21ldGhpbmcgdG8geW91ciBw\r\ncm9qZWN0LWxvY2FsIC5ScHJvZmlsZSBsaWtlOjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZu\r\nYnNwOyBpZiAoZmlsZS5leGlzdHMoIn4vLlJwcm9maWxlIikpIHNvdXJjZSgifi8uUnByb2ZpbGUi\r\nKTwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+b3Igd2UgY291bGQgZXZlbiBjb25zaWRlciBhbGxv\r\nd2luZyB1c2VycyB0byBvcHQtaW4gdG8gc291cmNpbmcgdGhhdCBgLlJwcm9maWxlYCBvbiBgcGFj\r\na3JhdDo6aW5pdCgpYCAoaWUsIGF1dG9tYXRpY2FsbHkgYWRkaW5nIHRoYXQgY29kZSB0byB0aGUg\r\nYXV0by1sb2FkZXIpLjwvZGl2Pg==\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Jan 22, 2015 at 5:35 PM, Joe Cheng <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">j...@joecheng.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Sorry, I meant R_HOME/etc/Rprofile.site (note, no leading period on Rprofile.site).<div><a href=\"http://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/base/html/Startup.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/base/html/Startup.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242671604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Bmjl0FENOgzOhP8KUEJ7_\">http://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/base/html/Startup.html</a><br></div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Jan 22, 2015 at 5:31 PM, Joe Cheng <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">j...@joecheng.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Yasmin, if you&#39;re saying that you normally set the repo in ~/.Rprofile, I think you&#39;re right that packrat&#39;s per-project .Rprofile stops that from working. Can you use R_HOME/etc/Renviron.site instead?</div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Jan 22, 2015 at 3:56 PM, Kevin Ushey <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ke...@rstudio.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Hi Yasmin,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">When initializing a new project, packrat infers the repositories based on the current value of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">getOption(&#39;repos&#39;)</code>, and then caches those (in the lockfile) to be used later.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">It seems like you would be able to do such a thing with e.g. <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">options(repos = &lt;localRepos); packrat::init()</code>.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">For example, if I run:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">R --vanilla --slave -e &quot;options(repos = &#39;~/local/cran&#39;); packrat::init()&quot;\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I see in the generated lockfile:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">Repos: CRAN=~/local/cran\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">It sounds like this (or some version of this) should suffice for what you need.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Best,<br>Kevin</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgWWFzbWluLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+V2hlbiBpbml0aWFsaXppbmcgYSBuZXcgcHJv\r\namVjdCwgcGFja3JhdCBpbmZlcnMgdGhlIHJlcG9zaXRvcmllcyBiYXNlZCBvbiB0aGUgY3VycmVu\r\ndCB2YWx1ZSBvZiBgZ2V0T3B0aW9uKCdyZXBvcycpYCwgYW5kIHRoZW4gY2FjaGVzIHRob3NlIChp\r\nbiB0aGUgbG9ja2ZpbGUpIHRvIGJlIHVzZWQgbGF0ZXIuPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj5JdCBzZWVtcyBsaWtlIHlvdSB3b3VsZCBiZSBhYmxlIHRvIGRvIHN1Y2ggYSB0aGluZyB3aXRo\r\nIGUuZy4gYG9wdGlvbnMocmVwb3MgPSAmbHQ7bG9jYWxSZXBvcyk7IHBhY2tyYXQ6OmluaXQoKWAu\r\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5Gb3IgZXhhbXBsZSwgaWYgSSBydW46PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7IFIgLS12YW5pbGxhIC0tc2xhdmUgLWUgIm9w\r\ndGlvbnMocmVwb3MgPSAnfi9sb2NhbC9jcmFuJyk7IHBhY2tyYXQ6OmluaXQoKSI8L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pkkgc2VlIGluIHRoZSBnZW5lcmF0ZWQgbG9ja2ZpbGU6PC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7IFJlcG9zOiBDUkFOPX4vbG9jYWwvY3Jhbjwv\r\nZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+SXQgc291bmRzIGxpa2UgdGhpcyAob3Igc29tZSB2ZXJz\r\naW9uIG9mIHRoaXMpIHNob3VsZCBzdWZmaWNlIGZvciB3aGF0IHlvdSBuZWVkLjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+\r\nPGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+QmVzdCw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PktldmluPC9kaXY+\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\">​</div></div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Jan 22, 2015 at 11:09 AM, Yasmin Lucero <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yasmin...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve seen this: <div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242671604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MwoOQaoaNsbf6LjszyPRm\">http://rstudio.github.io/packrat/custom-repos.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>But this requires me to set my repo option after initializing a new project. I would like to be able to set a system configuration so that all new projects default to only knowing about our local repository, unless explicitly told about an external CRAN mirror. Packrat seems to stomp on my system .Rprofile file. Am I missing something?</div></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;packrat-discuss&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">packrat-discu...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242671604000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1FY1HU_E6R4pDVlFdtHAUy\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;packrat-discuss&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">packrat-discu...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242671604000&a